# SAME70Q20B USB-CDC boot/connect smoke test in DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE
# (the tick-lockstep sibling of same70_usb_smoke, which runs free-run).
# Boots the CONFIG_ATSAM_USB firmware variant under Renode against the
# local USBHS peripheral (test/emulator/repl/same70_usbhs.cs), completes
# klippy identify + clocksync + config over the synthetic BULK_IN/BULK_OUT
# pipe Renode exposes as a pty (UARTBase) - but with the host<->mcu link
# riding tick lockstep through identify rather than free-running.
#
# Why this is now possible: in tick mode klippy's reactor advances
# simulated time one quantum per host<->mcu round trip. The renode launcher
# RunFor's exactly that quantum. Until now the renode pty did not register
# the serialqueue_need_prompt predicate (only the simavr AF_UNIX socket
# did), so the reactor advanced a full QMAX (100 ms) per round trip and a
# ~250-chunk identify dictionary scan cost ~25 s of simulated time - orders
# of magnitude longer than real hardware, with the connect window unable to
# close. klippy/serialhdl.py now registers need_prompt for every tick MCU,
# so identify/clock-sync round trips advance at the small QWAIT (8 ms)
# quantum and the dictionary scan completes promptly. need_prompt only
# gates the quantum; the renode receive still rides its background thread.
DICTIONARY same70q20b-usb.dict
CONFIG same70_usb_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR same70_usb_tick.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
M105

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
